From: MediaTek Inc.
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: hnat: add bridge and multi-WAN offload support

Add support for hardware flow offloading through bridge interfaces (e.g. br-wan,
br-lan), enabling WAN blind-plugging (e.g. bridging 2.5G RJ45 and 10G SFP WAN ports)
and PPPoE/DHCP over bridge without requiring Linux bonding.

Key features:
1. Dynamically identify WAN interfaces (wan, sfp-wan, br-wan, pppoe-*) and LAN
   interfaces (lan*, sfp-lan, br-lan, bond*) instead of strict name prefix match.
2. Resolve bridge master interfaces to underlying physical egress ports via FDB
   lookup (br_fdb_find_rcu) for both PPPoE and routed/bridged traffic.
3. Automatically enable GMAC PPE forwarding on all bridge member ports when bridge
   is brought UP.
4. Flush bound PPE entries when a bridge port drops carrier, enabling fast and
   seamless WAN blind-plugging failover between RJ45 and SFP ports.
5. Prevent invalid netdev_priv() access on bridge net_device instances.

Signed-off-by: MediaTek Inc.
